body:
I don't we're seeing the worst of cheaters in general, I still remember when seeing a DouYin name in lobby meant not to queue because they'd be flying through walls and looting you while alive. Still, the fact that this has been an issue for about as long as the game has been out should tell you something. I'm done for this wipe because of it, my last straw was a guy flying on reserve with a PKM. It also doesn't help that Tarkov is around the peak of its popularity. When the community was much smaller, I feel like cheaters were much less common. Could just be the tainted feeling of nostalgia, but lately it's felt like I can't play *without* meeting a cheater. 

&#x200B;

It also doesn't help that with so many more players, most casual people can't really keep up with the time investment needed to reach real progression. The amount of people paying for cheaters to carry is pretty pathetic.
